    rationale: `Gottman describes flooding as diffuse physiological arousal: a racing heart and surge of stress hormones that make it hard to listen, think or respond with empathy. Flooded partners often stonewall or escalate. Couples are taught to recognize flooding, take a break of at least 20 minutes doing something soothing, and then return to the conversation.`,
